@startuml
title P2P Infrastructure - Class Diagram

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
left to right direction

package "shared-core - P2P Infrastructure" {

    class P2PSearchController <<Controller>>

    class DistributedSearchService <<Service>> {
        + distributedSearch(...)
    }

    interface LocalSearchProvider

    class PeerClient <<HTTP Client>> {
        + forwardSearch(...)
    }

    class PeerRegistry <<Registry>>

    class PeerNode <<Model>>

    class DistributedSearchRequest <<DTO>> {
        + requestId
        + path
        + ttl
        + nextHop()
    }

    class SearchRequestTracker <<Service>>

    class JsonResponseAggregator <<Service>>

    class PeerTokenService <<Security>>

    class PeerAuthenticationFilter <<Security>>

    class P2PSecurityConfig <<Configuration>>

    class PeerRegistryInitializer <<Configuration>>

    class P2PConfig <<Configuration>>
}

package "airports-routes-service" {
    class AirportLocalSearchProvider <<Adapter>>
    class SearchAirportUseCase <<Application>>
}

P2PSearchController --> DistributedSearchService : delegates search

DistributedSearchService --> LocalSearchProvider : searches locally
DistributedSearchService --> PeerRegistry : discovers peers
DistributedSearchService --> PeerClient : forwards requests
DistributedSearchService --> SearchRequestTracker : detects duplicates
DistributedSearchService --> JsonResponseAggregator : merges responses
DistributedSearchService --> DistributedSearchRequest : processes

PeerRegistry "1" o-- "*" PeerNode : maintains
PeerClient --> PeerTokenService : generates JWT
PeerClient --> DistributedSearchRequest : forwards

PeerAuthenticationFilter --> PeerTokenService : validates JWT
P2PSecurityConfig --> PeerAuthenticationFilter : configures

PeerRegistryInitializer --> PeerRegistry : registers peers

AirportLocalSearchProvider ..|> LocalSearchProvider : implements
AirportLocalSearchProvider --> SearchAirportUseCase : executes

note bottom of DistributedSearchService
Coordinates local and remote searches.
Uses TTL and request tracking
to limit forwarding and loops.
end note

@enduml
